{"name": "Barkot", "slug": "barkot", "type": "destination", "curatedDistrict": "Uttarkashi", "region": "Garhwal", "location": "", "category": "", "highlightCandidates": ["Yamunotri", "Barkot"], "articleTitle": "Barkot, Uttarakhand", "site": "wikipedia", "wikidataQid": "Q2552248", "coords": {"lat": 30.82, "lon": 78.2}, "onPageImages": ["File:Barkot With Bandarpunch.jpg", "File:Flag of India.svg", "File:India Uttarakhand location map.svg", "File:India Uttaranchal locator map.svg", "File:India location map.svg", "File:Question book-new.svg", "File:Red pog.svg"], "pageimage": "Barkot_With_Bandarpunch.jpg", "pageUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barkot,_Uttarakhand", "extract": "Barkot is a town and nagar palika near Uttarkashi, Uttarkashi District in the state of Uttarakhand, India. It is located on the banks of the Yamuna river. Tiladi Sera village in the tehsil was the location of the infamous Tiladi massacre in 1930.\n\n\nGeography\nBarkot is located at 30.82°N 78.20°E﻿ / 30.82; 78.20. It has an average elevation of 1,220 metres (4,003 feet).\nBarkot is located on the bank of Yamuna river. \n\n\nDemographics\nAs of the 2001 India census, Barkot had a population of 16,568. Males constitute 53% of the population and females 47%. Barkot has an average literacy rate of 84.5%, higher than the national average of 74%; with 93% of the males and 77% of females literate. 54% of the population is under 6 years of age.\n\n\nReferences\n\n\nExternal links\nBarkot at WikiMapia", "wikivoyageExtract": null, "wikidataDistrict": ["Q1773437"], "coverImage": {"url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a7/Barkot_With_Bandarpunch.jpg", "source": "Wikimedia Commons", "sourcePage": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barkot_With_Bandarpunch.jpg", "license": "CC0 (http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en)", "attribution": "See file page for author/credits", "alt": "Barkot, Uttarakhand"}, "coverImageLowerResolution": false, "gallery": [{"url": "https://t